                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Peachtree City GA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 5 at 1:21AM EST until November 5 at 2:30AM EST by NWS Peachtree City GA",
                "description": "FFWFFC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Peachtree City has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthwestern Fannin County in north central Georgia...\nNorth Central Gilmer County in north central Georgia...\n\n* Until 230 AM EST.\n\n* At 121 AM EST, local law enforcement reported thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 5 and 6 inches\nof rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1.5 to 2.5\ninches in 1 hour. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing.\n\nFLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY for Southern Fannin and Northern Gilmer. This\nis a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER GROUND NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER\nGROUND NOW! Life threatening flash flooding of low water\ncrossings, small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBlue Ridge, Higdon and Colwell.",
                "instruction": "Move to higher ground now! This is an extremely dangerous and\nlife-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are\nfleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
